=== Suspension ===
The CTR3 utilizes [[MacPherson strut|MacPherson strut suspension]] on the front axle from the Porsche 911, and [[multi-link suspension]] with horizontal coil over shock absorbers at the rear axle. [[Anti-roll bar|Anti-roll bars]] are installed on both axles.<ref name=evo />

=== Wheels ===
The CTR3 is equipped with forged aluminum wheels with diameters of 19 inches at the front and 20 inches at the rear. The tires are [[Michelin]] Pilot Super Sports with [[Tire code|codes]] of 255/35 ZR 19 for the front and 335/30 ZR 20 for the rear. The brakes are ventilated ceramic composite discs, with a diameter of 380mm each and utilizing six-piston aluminium calipers at the front and rear.<ref name=evo /><ref name=ss>{{cite web|url=http://www.superstreetonline.com/features/1311-2014-ruf-ctr3-club-sport/|website=Super Street Network|title=2014 Ruf CTR3 Club Sport - Ruf Trade|first=Ian|last=Kuah|date=2013-10-30|accessdate=2018-08-14}}</ref>

==Performance==
The CTR3 has claimed acceleration times of 0-{{convert|60|mph|0|abbr=on}} in 3.2 seconds, with an estimated top speed of {{convert|233|mph|km/h|abbr=on|0}}.<ref name="r&t" /> The extra {{convert|86|hp|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|91|Nm|0|abbr=on}} of torque in the Clubsport reduce its 0-{{convert|60|mph|0|abbr=on}} time to 3.0 seconds, with an estimated top speed of {{convert|236|mph|km/h|abbr=on|0}}.<ref name="thedrive2">{{Cite web |last=Burkart |first=Tom |date=2014-09-10 |title=777HP, 236MPH 2015 RUF CTR3 Clubsport Is Veyron-Hunting, Twin-Turbo Cayman |url=http://www.car-revs-daily.com/2014/09/10/ruf-ctr3-clubsport/ |access-date=2018-08-15 |website=TheDrive}}</ref>

==CTR3 Clubsport==
[[File:2013 RUF CTR3 Clubsport SP25.jpg|thumb|2013 Ruf CTR3 Clubsport]]
Ruf unveiled the CTR3 Clubsport variant at the [[Geneva Motor Show|2012 Geneva Motor Show]] as an evolution and replacement of the standard CTR3.<ref name=gtspirit>{{Cite web|url=https://gtspirit.com/2012/03/07/geneva-2012-ruf-ctr3-clubsport/|title=Geneva 2012: RUF CTR3 Clubsport|last=Adams|first=Lawrence|date=2012-03-07|website=GulfWeekly|access-date=2018-08-15}}</ref> The Clubsport features a revised engine with power boosted to {{convert|777|PS|kW hp|0|abbr=on}} at 7,000 rpm and a maximum torque of {{convert|980|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} at 4,000 rpm.<ref name=rufofficial>{{Cite web|url=https://ruf-automobile.de/en/modell/ctr3-clubsport/|title=The RUF model with pure super sports car DNA|website=Ruf Automobile|access-date=2018-08-15}}</ref> The Clubsport also introduced an optional 7-speed [[dual-clutch transmission]] in addition to the standard 6-speed sequential manual. As of May 2018, only 7 CTR3 Clubsport cars have been built in addition to 30 standard CTR3 cars.<ref name=thedrive>{{Cite web|url=https://www.thedrive.com/news/20539/one-of-the-last-ruf-ctr-3-clubsports-is-going-to-auction-in-monaco|title=One of the Last RUF CTR 3 Clubsports is Going to Auction in Monaco|last=Constantine|first=Chris|date=2018-04-30|website=TheDrive|access-date=2018-08-15}}</ref>

The CTR3 Clubsport shares many features with the [[Lykan HyperSport]], a car developed from the same engine.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.evo.co.uk/news/18930/lykan-hypersport-all-you-need-to-know|title=Lykan Hypersport: all you need to know|first=Jordan|last=Katsianis|website=evo|date=February 23, 2017|accessdate=August 13, 2018}}</ref> Among these similarities are: engine (3.7L twin-turbo flat-six), transmissions (6-speed sequential manual and 7-speed [[Dual-clutch transmission#Porsche (VW GROUP)|PDK]]), suspension (MacPherson strut front and multi-link rear), wheels, tyres and brakes (255/35 ZR 19 for the front, 335/30 ZR 20 for the rear, 380mm carbon ceramic discs), weight (1,377 kg for the CTR3 and 1,380 kg for the Hypersport), and physical dimensions (height and length are within 35mm, wheelbase and width are identical at 2,625mm and 1,944mm respectively).

== CTR3 Evo ==
Ruf unveiled the CTR3 Evo at the 2023 [[Monterey Car Week]] as an evolution of the CTR3 Clubsport. The Evo has a tuned version of the [[Porsche flat-six engine|3.8L twin turbo flat six]] from the Clubsport, with power increased to {{Convert|800|PS|kW hp|0|abbr=on}} at 7100 rpm and {{Convert|730|lbft|0|abbr=on|order=flip}} of torque at 4000 rpm.<ref>{{Cite web |title=RUF Automobile: The RUF CTR3 Evo |url=https://www.ruf-automobile.de/en/modelle/ctr3-evo/ |access-date=2024-01-12 |website=www.ruf-automobile.de |language=en}}</ref> Ruf claims a top speed of {{Convert|236|mph|0|abbr=on}} for the Evo. It also features tweaked bodywork, including new front and rear bumpers, and the Cayman taillights of previous CTR3 models being replaced with circular units.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Perkins |first=Chris |title=The 800-HP RUF CTR3 Evo Is RUF's Most Powerful Car Yet |url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/news/a44839495/ruf-ctr3-evo/}}</ref>

